-# What happens to a template rwr cannot stitch into Ruby? HAML introduces its
-# Ruby with a leading `=` or `-` rather than with delimiters, so there is
-# nothing to translate and the account of it can only come from text search.
-# That is a weaker claim than the rest of the report and has to arrive labelled
-# as one -- but silence would be worse, because a rename that misses a view
-# under-reports, which is the dangerous direction.
%table.accounts
  %thead
    %tr
      -# GT:ignore -- a translation key, which text search cannot tell from a call
      %th= t("accounts.display_name")
  %tbody
    - @accounts.each do |account|
      %tr
        -# GT:residue -- reached by text search, in a template with no delimiters
        %td= account.display_name
        %td= account.email
